+
+  /// Asks the window itself, now, whether it is in the Dock, on its way there, or gone. What was last reported does not tell: an app can
+  /// name its next window half a second before it says that the one in use has been minimized, and `focus` fetches a window out
+  /// of the Dock. Asked to take the keyboard in that half second it flies there and straight back, and its person's ⌘M is undone.
+  /// True as well where its app does not answer: what cannot be found out is no leave to act. No default: in a wrapper that
+  /// forgot to pass it on, windows would come back out of the Dock in silence.
+  func isInTheDockOrGone(_ window: WindowID) -> Bool
 }
 
